import pandas as pd

# Load the dataset from the last assignment 'cleaned box office data'
enhanced_box_office = pd.read_csv("enhanced_box_office_data(2000-2024)u.csv")

# Load the new data set 'Marvel Movies'
marvel_movies = pd.read_csv("Marvel Movies.csv")

# Merge the datasets on 'Year' (box office) and 'year' (Marvel movies)
merged_data = enhanced_box_office.merge(marvel_movies, left_on='Year', right_on='year', how='left')

# Save the merged dataset
merged_data.to_csv("merged_box_office_marvel.csv", index=False)

### Explanation

### Merge Strategy Explanation
I used a left join to merge the datasets because it ensures that all rows from the `enhanced_box_office` dataset are retained, and matching rows from the `Marvel Movies` dataset are added where available.

#### Handling NA Values
If there are years in the box office dataset that do not have corresponding records in the Marvel dataset, those rows will have `NaN` values in the Marvel-specific columns. This prevents loss of any box office data while still incorporating available Marvel movie details.
